  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday night through next Tuesday)\nIssued at 240 PM CDT Tue Sep 29 2026\n\nAs was mentioned in the short discussion, models show some \nuncertainty regarding how quickly the heaviest precipitation \nadvances eastward by Thursday night. Some of the guidance shows \nthe bulk of precipitation exiting far southeast counties Thursday \nafternoon, while others show heavy precipitation lingering through\nThursday night. For now, will maintain high POPs over the eastern\nportions of the Heartland and northwest Hill Country Thursday \nnight and early Friday. While the threat for heavy rainfall will \ncome to an end by Friday, a weak trough will reside over the area \nover the weekend, which will keep low to medium (20 to 60%) rain \nchances lingering over the weekend. In addition, below normal \ntemperatures are expected Friday through early next week, with \nhighs in the 70s through Monday. Overnight lows will be in the \nupper 50s and lower 60s.",
